            "finding": {
              "summary": "The East depot has conflicting reserve stock requirements: P1 mandates a minimum of 20 reserve pallets to cover supply interruptions, while P3 limits the maximum to 12 pallets to maintain fire-lane clearance. This creates a direct conflict between inventory and capacity policies. The operational risk arises from potential stockouts due to insufficient reserves or safety hazards from overcrowding, depending on which policy is enforced. The conflicting thresholds are 20 (minimum) and 12 (maximum) reserve pallets. Conflicting requirements: inventory-policy says \"The East depot must keep at least twenty reserve pallets on site to cover supply interruptions.\"; capacity-policy says \"The East depot may keep at most twelve reserve pallets on site to maintain fire-lane clearance.\"; inventory-policy says \"Reducing reserve stock requires the inventory owner's approval.\"; capacity-policy says \"The capacity owner must review any proposed exception.\" Ask the responsible policy owners to review the conflict together and document a resolution before changing operations. The cited passages do not establish which requirement takes precedence.",
